//RS //! Offline stage-zero repackaging.
//RS //!
//RS //! `stage0-repack <keep-dir> [<compiler-project>]` reruns only the Host/Runner
//RS //! packaging half of stage zero (`emit_stage_zero_source` after MIR Rust
//RS //! emission) from what a `JET_STAGE_ZERO_KEEP=<keep-dir>` run retained:
//RS //!
//RS //! - `reference.rs`: the unpackaged emitted Rust of the compiler,
//RS //! - `stage-zero.image`: the compiler image, which holds the canonical MIR
//RS //!   program, the compiler artifact, the factory root and the source-authority
//RS //!   digest,
//RS //! - `stage-zero.ffi`: the FFI bridge crate the emitted Rust names,
//RS //! - the authorized compiler sources, whose authority digest the image binds:
//RS //!   the second argument, else `<keep-dir>/compiler-project` when the run
//RS //!   retained it, else the shared assembly
//RS //!   `~/.cache/jet-luna/compiler-bootstrap/project`.
//RS //!
//RS //! It writes the fresh packaged source to `<keep-dir>/stage-zero.rs` and into
//RS //! the kept backend project `<keep-dir>/stage-zero/` (`generated.rs`,
//RS //! `src/main.rs`, `src/compiler.image` when the image changed). The unit
//RS //! crates are a function of `reference.rs` alone, so only the main crate
//RS //! changes.
//RS //!
//RS //! The harness `main` appended after packaging is `GENERATED_ARTIFACT_MAIN`
//RS //! of the generator sources' `Compiler/Bootstrap/Tests.rs`, task-root regions
//RS //! stripped unless the kept `stage-zero.stamp` says `task_roots=true`; it is
//RS //! also written to `artifact-main.rs`. The first run derives
//RS //! `stage-zero/main.prefix.rs` (the main crate's text before the packaged
//RS //! suffix) from the kept run's own output, which is only sound while the
//RS //! generators still produce it. It keeps the kept run's source as
//RS //! `stage-zero.base.rs` and reports whether the fresh source is
//RS //! byte-identical to it.
//RS 
//RS #![allow(non_snake_case)]
//RS 
